{
  "$comment": [
    "Get the QSPI vias OUT of U2's pads. This repairs a regression U6 introduced:",
    "routing the bus bottom-side let the router drop its escape vias straight into",
    "the flash's SMD pads, where an unplugged barrel wicks solder away from the",
    "joint during reflow. The pre-U6 layout had them correctly outside, and the",
    "west-column positions here are the original ones, which were DRC-clean.",
    "",
    "KiCad's DRC does not flag via-in-pad, and neither did the length/via/layer",
    "measurements U6 verified against -- it took kicad-happy's pad audit to see it.",
    "Worth remembering: 'DRC clean and measured' is not the same as 'assemblable'.",
    "",
    "West column escapes west into the lane between the Inner2 keepout edge",
    "(x=166.129) and the pads (x=167.090). CLK escapes EAST instead, because U6",
    "brought it down the north-east side rather than along the west lane. East",
    "column escapes west into the gap between U2's thermal pad (east edge 173.915)",
    "and the east pads (west edge 175.090), with the two verticals staggered to",
    "174.35 and 174.75 so they clear each other and both pad columns."
  ],
